WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.320
Hello, everyone!

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.720
If you’re a fan of SCP Explained, you’ll
know that we regularly post interesting questions

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.329
in our community tab, asking for responses
from you - our dear fans.

00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:17.890
These have ranged from questions about specific
anomalies, like SCP-096, or your suggestions

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:23.089
on how we should actually kill SCP-682, the
Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:27.539
We’ve even asked you which anomalous powers
you’d want to have, and posed your questions

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:34.899
directly to SCP-343, also known as God, and
of course, the terrifying and infamous Scarlet

00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:35.899
King.

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:40.260
But in our latest community question, asking
you about hypothetical crossovers between

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.699
the SCP Foundation and the weird, wild multiverse
of all fiction, you truly outdid yourself,

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:49.370
with thousands upon thousands of responses.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.730
And we thought, rather than just making one
video selecting our favorites, we’d turn

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.280
each of our favorites into whole videos.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.490
And how are we going to do that?

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.399
That’s when this wonderful state-of-the-art
gizmo comes into play!

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:07.740
You may remember the Anom-O-Tron 6000, our
incredibly advanced artificial intelligence-driven

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:12.600
supercomputer designed specifically to run
simulations for the SCP Foundation.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.730
We’ve fed this computer data from countless
SCP Foundation experiments and cross tests,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.610
and all the data from your suggestions.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.799
This will allow the fine folks at the SCP
Foundation to explore any anomalous hypothetical,

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:29.299
without risking the lives of staff members
or civilians.

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:35.750
This brings us to our first simulation, suggested
in a huge number of comments: Could SCP-682

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.890
be Contained Within the Backrooms?

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.870
For those not in the know, the Backrooms is
an internet urban legend that’s spiraled

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.729
into a full-blown phenomenon.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:50.439
It’s built on the premise that if you’re
not careful and enter certain specific circumstances,

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:56.700
you can no clip out of our reality, and enter
a terrifying, multi-level alternate reality,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.590
where you’re stalked by a variety of bizarre
and frightening creatures.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.970
This could be a complete nightmare for your
average person, but how would it play out

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:11.150
if SCP-682, the endlessly angry Hard to Destroy
Reptile, found its way inside?

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:16.420
Also, for another Backrooms-related surprise,
stick around until the end of the video…

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.200
In the meantime, though, let’s boot up the
Anom-O-Tron and test this new scenario!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.180
The worst had happened: Again.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:29.030
SCP-682 had busted out of containment during
a cross test and started making a beeline

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.260
for the nearest populated area.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.530
Several helicopters containing heavily-armed
MTF Nu-7, “Hammer Down”, members were

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.470
in hot pursuit, attempting to slow the vicious
reptile down with targeted sniper fire at

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.690
its legs.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.900
But it seemed that these efforts were all
for naught: SCP-682 had already reached the

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.760
defunct industrial district on the edge of
a nearby city, and if the beast managed to

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.780
actually reach a populated area, all hell
would break loose.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.900
That’s when they pulled out the heavy weaponry:
Miniguns mounted to the helicopters unleashed

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.760
a rain of hellfire down onto SCP-682.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:09.930
However, 682 managed to dodge most of the
bullets and simply tank the rest.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.780
Command authorized the use of heavy ordinance:
The helicopter’s missile launches.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:19.240
They’d pick up the pieces afterwards, once
SCP-682 was back in containment.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.140
However, the reptile had plans of its own.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.400
It charged into a nearby abandoned chemical
plant to avoid the gunfire from above.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.880
This was exactly what Hammer Down wanted.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.010
The helicopters circled around the chemical
plant and unleashed a barrage of powerful

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:39.820
incendiary missiles, blowing the plant to
kingdom come in hopes of dragging an incapacitated

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.020
682 out of the rubble afterwards.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:48.730
But when the smoke had cleared and only the
rubble was left, 682 was nowhere to be seen.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.480
Even for the hardcore operatives of Hammer
Down, this caused an anxiety spike.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.210
Had it tunneled into the ground?

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.250
Had it adapted to the attack by turning invisible
or getting tiny to escape?

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.800
It’d done all these things before.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.530
Or after all the deranged attempts at putting
SCP-682 in the ground, had some light firebombing

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.940
killed the monster?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.550
Whatever the case, they’d need to search,
in case SCP-682 popped up somewhere else and

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.940
started causing havoc.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:20.870
If it was still alive - which it probably
was - they couldn’t rest on their laurels

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.940
until they’d found it again.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.120
Meanwhile, SCP-682 woke up.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.250
It felt groggy and irritated, its body resting
against an unpleasant, soggy carpet.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:36.470
It licked the carpet - the moisture had the
distinct flavor of human spinal fluid, which

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.980
682 had tasted many times before.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.210
The sickly yellow walls and incessant buzzing
from the fluorescent lights up above were

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:47.090
nauseating, and it gave 682 a nagging headache.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:52.290
This only made 682’s default emotion - blistering
rage and hatred - even worse.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.000
It began walking around, exploring this strange,
spatially anomalous environment.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.250
Was this more of that frustrating Foundation
trickery?

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.860
Another one of those puerile “cross-tests”?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.080
The last thing 682 remembered was running
at one of the walls in the chemical plant

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.160
- a wall that, in hindsight, seemed darker
than the others - but rather than shattering

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.260
through the brickwork, it was here now, in
this strange, tacky lobby that never seemed

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.260
to end.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:22.470
It was like a kaleidoscope of empty, 1990s
office kitsch.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:27.330
Endless worthless yellow walls arranged like
some labyrinthine, nonsensical maze, leading

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.530
nowhere and devoid of all life as SCP-682
wandered through it.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:36.380
And of course, SCP-682 found it disgusting.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:42.760
It was only on Level 0, and already, 682 hated
the Backrooms just as much as it hated our

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.960
dimension.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:49.770
Someone or something had to pay for the crime
of inconveniencing it this way, and it would

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:55.700
happily turn this whole dimension inside out
just to find some beings to kill inside it.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.880
Yes, that would be great fun…

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:04.060
SCP-682 began its frantic search for an exit,
evolving an innate sonar ability and picking

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.490
up speeds that would be impossible for human
beings.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:12.090
This is the part where most people would go
mad, or die from hunger or thirst.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.500
SCP-682?

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:14.500
Not so much.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:19.850
It could keep searching, and searching, and
searching until the stars burned out in the

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.850
sky.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:26.250
It would find its prey, somehow, and when
it did, it would put them through hell.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:31.420
And as it turned out, this new universe rewarded
682’s dogged stubbornness, because when

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.750
it passed through a seemingly random hallway
after hours of searching, it was in a different

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.390
place entirely.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:42.020
This place looked like some huge abandoned
warehouse complex with water shining off the

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.020
ground.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.930
If 682 had more advanced knowledge of the
Backrooms, it would have known this was Level

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:47.930
1.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:53.210
But the only number SCP-682 cared about was
body count, and in that regard, it would find

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.389
Level 1 to be a vast improvement.

00:06:56.389 --> 00:07:00.840
Two groups of humans had established bases
in this level of the Backrooms: The Major

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.450
Explorer Group, a faction of professional
Backrooms traversers who maintained their

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:09.480
Base Alpha on this level, and the Backrooms
Nonaligned Trade Group, a commercial group

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:14.889
whose primary base is an economic hub on this
very level - A fortified city-like area with

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:22.590
a population of 412, which would, a few hours
after 682’s appearance, be a population

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:23.590
of zero.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:26.430
But before all that, it felt like grabbing
a bite at the diner…

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:30.980
Tom’s Diner is a refuge for many people
trapped in the backrooms - a casual eatery

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:35.610
nestled into the cold warehouse environment
of Level 1, where people could get a warm

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:40.720
meal from Tom, a former cook who’s been
trapped in the Backroom for years.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.560
SCP-682 was eager to be a part of this grand
tradition - But the Hard to Destroy Reptile

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:49.960
decided to buck the trend a little by just
devouring Tom himself.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:54.860
From there, it decided to launch its rage-fueled
offensive against the various humanoid inhabitants

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.060
of the level.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.199
Both the Major Explorers Group Base Alpha
and the Backrooms Nonaligned Trade Group Trade

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:05.050
Keep were heavily fortified against the kind
of entities these folks had gotten used to

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:11.040
facing in The Backrooms, but they were completely
unprepared for a creature of SCP-682’s sheer

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.220
power, intelligence, endurance, and ferocity.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.050
The SCP Foundation had been studying the creature
for decades, with far more resources than

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:23.470
either of these two Backrooms-bound groups,
and they still had a hard time keeping the

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:25.930
beast consistently contained.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:31.160
Sadly for the greatest bastions of human hope
in the Backrooms, SCP-682 swept through both

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:36.110
outposts in a matter of hours, killing everyone
there without an ounce of remorse.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:40.620
The only person there it took its time with
was the final human being left in the decimated

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.010
remains of the Major Explorers Group Base
Alpha.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:48.800
It grabbed the man by the throat and squeezed,
asking with its guttural, growing voice:

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:49.800
“You.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:56.080
Were you and your dead brethren allied with
the SCP Foundation?”

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:00.940
Despite his fear, the Explorer told 682 that
he had never heard of the SCP Foundation.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.270
Nor did he know what kind of entity 682 was.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.270
“Hmm.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.290
Then what is this place?

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:12.330
Tell me, and I might give you a quick death.”

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:17.890
The Explorer gave as good a response as he
could: 682 was trapped in the Backrooms, a

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:21.710
multi-level interdimensional nightmare filled
with dangerous creatures.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.550
That made 682 curious - Dangerous creatures?

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:27.190
That could make an interesting challenge.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:32.640
682 asked the Explorer how it could access
these other levels, and find these creatures,

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.480
and the Explorer explained that through exploring
these levels enough, anyone could “no clip”

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.920
into the next one.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.620
It really was that simple.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:45.650
With that, 682 knew all it needed to know
and carelessly murdered the final human being

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:46.700
of Level 1.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.270
It had killed so many humans over its long
and twisted life - It was no different from

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.839
breathing air now, an utterly perfunctory
action.

00:09:54.839 --> 00:09:59.211
It was eager to discover these other creatures
on the lower levels, and teach them a new

00:09:59.211 --> 00:10:02.480
level of fear they’d never experienced…

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:07.740
682 stormed through the halls until it achieved
the next successful no clip into Level 2,

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.890
which manifested as a series of old, dilapidated
maintenance tunnels that seemed to stretch

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.899
on for millions of miles.

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:14.940
Wonderful.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:18.680
There were humans here, too, apparently, but
who cared about them?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:23.800
This was the first level to feature a smorgasbord
of “Entities”, ripe for the killing.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:30.110
It sped through the tunnels, teeth, and fangs
borne, eager to deal death with gleeful abandon.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:34.740
The first entities it encountered in the expansive
tunnels of Level 2 were a collection of beings

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:40.540
known as Crawlers: Insect-like creatures infected
with an extremely aggressive fungal growth.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.851
Just getting close to them could present an
active risk to humans - Not so much for a

00:10:44.851 --> 00:10:48.810
creature that could easily regenerate after
being tossed into the sun.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:53.730
As the creatures tried to lunge, SCP-682 simply
crushed and devoured them with little effort.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:58.370
They tasted a little stale, on account of
the fungus, but the chewiness was pleasing.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:02.830
Hopefully, there would be more challenging
foes down in the tunnel than these mere insects,

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:08.970
SCP-682 thought to itself while journeying
deeper into the endless network of tunnels.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:14.410
Soon enough, SCP-682 ventured into a section
of the tunnel engulfed in total darkness.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.779
Its eyes quickly adjusted, developing immaculate
night vision.

00:11:17.779 --> 00:11:22.220
That’s when it spotted another creature
sharing this little slice of darkness with

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:28.089
it: A pair of floating, glowing eyes and almost
cartoonish teeth, grinning like some maniacal

00:11:28.089 --> 00:11:29.430
Looney Tune.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:34.390
This is an entity known as a Smiler, and they’re
a terrifying threat to any humans venturing

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.270
through the Backrooms.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.270
SCP-682…

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:39.089
Wasn’t impressed.

00:11:39.089 --> 00:11:44.030
It began a perfect adaptation for the situation:
Its body began to glow, emitting incredible

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:48.230
levels of both heat and light, carving through
the darkness of the tunnel and causing the

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:51.170
Smiler to emit a terrible, piercing shriek.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:57.310
The sheer heat of this new ability melted
sections of the Level 2 tunnels around SCP-682.

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.720
When the light finally dimmed down to slightly
more reasonable levels, where the Smiler once

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:05.520
stood was instead a fizzling black scorch
mark.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:10.970
Another creature had painfully bitten the
dust, and SCP-682 was starting to have some

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:11.970
fun.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.830
It took off further down into the tunnels,
looking forward to finding its next victim.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:21.920
Sadly for SCP-682, it wouldn’t get to kill
the next set of victims.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:26.890
A group of four Child Facelings - spooky,
faceless little girls who like to cut apart

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:32.260
their typically human victims with small objects
- were waiting a little further down the pipe.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:37.490
However, when they felt SCP-682 approaching,
they almost sensed the power and cruelty of

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.089
the beast coming towards them.

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:44.580
Even being little monsters themselves, game
recognized game, and they knew that they needed

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.520
to get the hell out of there before the monster
arrived.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:51.450
They climbed between the pipes on the tunnel
walls and skittered off into hiding places

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.450
deep in the dark.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:56.899
Lucky for them, SCP-682 passed them and just
kept going.

00:12:56.899 --> 00:13:01.399
What would be the point in wasting time on
these little morsels when there were apparently

00:13:01.399 --> 00:13:04.930
so many other creatures to massacre down here?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:09.920
Next, SCP-682 came across a truly pathetic
creature - Something that the mighty reptile

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.870
honestly felt a little embarrassed even interacting
with.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:16.779
It was a creature known as a “Clump”,
a strange bundle of living limbs that will

00:13:16.779 --> 00:13:20.550
move at great speeds and attack its usually
human targets.

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:26.680
It tried to do the same to SCP-682, manically
flailing its many twisted limbs.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:31.600
682 killed it in a single stomp and moved
on, feeling its own psychological equivalent

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:34.224
of pity - but not that much of it.

00:13:34.224 --> 00:13:39.749
Not long after mercy-killing the Clump, SCP-682
came face to face with a series of Hounds

00:13:39.749 --> 00:13:45.280
- mutant humanoids who travel on all fours,
behaving in a wolf-like fashion.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:49.890
This would, of course, be the stuff of nightmares
for your average human being, but would be

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:54.850
far more likely to put a being like the Hard
to Destroy Reptile to sleep with sheer boredom.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.529
Humans acting like dogs?

00:13:56.529 --> 00:14:02.050
That makes them even more worthless, the creature
thought, as it charged forwards and began

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:04.500
tearing the group of Hounds to shreds.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.420
Minutes later, it was splitting off into an
adjoining tunnel, searching for more easy

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.500
entertainment.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:15.610
But the deeper SCP-682 made its way into the
bowels of Level 2, the more it approached

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:21.700
a truly horrifying realization: The creatures
it was slaughtering here were even more boring

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:26.810
than the ones the SCP Foundation ceaseless
threw at it back on its native reality - or

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:29.480
at least, the reality where they’d contained
it.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:34.870
Back in that world, it had faced giant, flaming
demi-gods with swords hotter than the sun.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.740
It had faced some pale, shrieking monstrosity
that didn’t seem to die no matter what the

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:40.230
reptile threw at it.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:44.740
There was the dark, gooey old man, the Immortal
Warrior from the Black Coffin, and even the

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.230
all-devouring bunny rabbit.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:52.350
Here, it was killing the same wretched selection
of beasts again and again, a truly pitiful

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.490
offering.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.150
Was this really the best this world had to
offer?

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:00.839
Incidentally, the next creatures it found
were literally known as the Wretches by the

00:15:00.839 --> 00:15:03.310
human inhabitants of The Backrooms.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:08.770
They were fleshy, zombie-like creatures that
682 figured the Sarkicists back home might

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:09.770
enjoy.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:13.950
It couldn’t believe it was thinking fondly
of that old place while it carved the monsters

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.870
to ribbons with its claws.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:21.470
It missed its old enemies, like Dr. Bright,
Dr. Clef, and even that irritating yellow

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:23.100
blob of snot.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.649
The more it tried to take its mind off the
old world by killing its way through this

00:15:26.649 --> 00:15:31.180
ant farm of endless tunnels, the more it found
itself waxing nostalgic.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:36.029
For example, there were the Plague Goblins,
impish little creatures with masks like that

00:15:36.029 --> 00:15:37.370
of a Plague Doctor.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:43.730
682 found itself thinking almost fondly about
SCP-049, while it listlessly ate the tiny,

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:48.890
mischievous creatures like a depressed person
binging an extra-large pack of chips.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:52.910
Even their tiny squeaks as they crunched between
the reptile’s terrible teeth gave it no

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:53.910
joy.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:57.279
What a bleak turn of events this had all turned
out to be.

00:15:57.279 --> 00:16:01.710
As it wandered through the infinite tunnels,
killing creatures and even humans as it found

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:08.490
them, SCP-682 made a quiet promise to itself:
Somehow, someway, it would make its way back

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:11.269
to the universe it’d so recently departed.

00:16:11.269 --> 00:16:16.850
It would leave the Backrooms, no matter how
many levels, a quiet, burning husk, and return

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:21.290
to the world of fools and fiends it had taken
for granted all this time.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:25.980
A visit to the Backrooms had taught the Hard
to Destroy Reptile an all-too-human lesson:

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.250
Sometimes, you don’t know what you have
until it’s gone.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:33.660
Sure, the SCP Foundation may have tried to
kill it in a new, bizarre, and increasingly

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:39.019
sadistic way every single day, but that variety
was the spice of life.

00:16:39.019 --> 00:16:44.079
It would return home someday, it knew that
much - But of course, a lot of creatures and

00:16:44.079 --> 00:16:46.740
people would need to die before then.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.519
But if that’s what it took, well, so be
it.

00:16:50.519 --> 00:16:54.470
SCP-682 licked its dagger-like fangs, and
kept crawling…

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:58.620
If you want more of our take on the bizarre
liminal hell that is The Backrooms, go check

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:03.360
out our new channel, The Backrooms - Explained,
for more Backrooms content in our signature

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.360
style!

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:09.909
Now go check out “SCP-682 - Ways SCP Foundation
Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy Reptile” and

00:17:09.909 --> 00:17:16.079
“SCP-682 vs SCP Foundation - Hard To Destroy
Reptile Termination Attempts” for more of

00:17:16.079 --> 00:17:18.319
everyone’s favorite ornery reptile!

